      "claim": "George Grimes was born on June 29, 1877 in Channel.",
      "answer": "June 29, 1877 in Channel",
      "quote": "Grimes George Frederick Arthur Grimes (June 29, 1877 – August 10, 1929) was a businessman and political figure in Newfoundland. He represented Port de Grave from 1913 to 1919, Fogo from 1923 to 1924, Twillingate from 1924 to 1928 and Lewisporte from 1928 to 1929 in the Newfoundland House of Assembly. He was born in Channel, the son of William Grimes and Amelia White.",
